{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1324935-lodge-of-the-field-details","id":1324935,"title":"Lodge of the Field details?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-07-16T05:06:04-07:00","id":1324935,"title":"Lodge of the Field details?","content":"Greetings,<br /> <br /> Just wondering if the Lodge of the Field will get a full treatment like those lodges in The Pack. As it is now it is downright powerful (and vague), I want to flesh them as antagonists: <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Lodge members gain double the usual Essence from consuming human flesh (<b>the Marrow Eater facet of the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/the-giver-of-gifts-2-werewolf-the-forsaken/\" target=\"_blank\">Gift of Essence</a></b> <b>already does this, or make them Bale Hounds of Consumption</b>), and every time they do so Lycaon himself gains a single point of Essence (<b>No idea what to do of this</b>).</li> <li>Lodge members add their Primal Urge to their maximum Essence pool. (<b>could be the Lodge Blessing</b>)</li> <li>Spending a point of Essence as an instant action allows a Hound to inflict gnawing hunger on a human whom she touches (<b>the Glutttony facet of the Gift of Hunger</b> <b>already does this</b>), and lodge members with very high Primal Urge can force spirits of hunger to Claim victims (<b>No idea what to do of this</b>)</li> </ol><br /> <br /> <br /> It seems that using the Gift of Hunger, Gift of Essence, Bale Hounds (Hounds of Consumption) <i>Siskur-Dah</i> and PERHAPS Ghost Wolf Devourers you get most of this lodge flavour. But what should be the Aspiration and Ban? What merits should they have? (I think Lodge Lorehouse and Lodge Stronghold are the most apt)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 07-16-2019, 04:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-26T19:08:55-07:00","id":1523194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1324935-lodge-of-the-field-details#post1324935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Greetings,<br /> <br /> Just wondering if the Lodge of the Field will get a full treatment like those lodges in The Pack. As it is now it is downright powerful (and vague), I want to flesh them as antagonists:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Lodge members gain double the usual Essence from consuming human flesh (<b>the Marrow Eater facet of the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/the-giver-of-gifts-2-werewolf-the-forsaken/\" target=\"_blank\">Gift of Essence</a></b> <b>already does this, or make them Bale Hounds of Consumption</b>), and every time they do so Lycaon himself gains a single point of Essence (<b>No idea what to do of this</b>).</li> <li>Lodge members add their Primal Urge to their maximum Essence pool. (<b>could be the Lodge Blessing</b>)</li> <li>Spending a point of Essence as an instant action allows a Hound to inflict gnawing hunger on a human whom she touches (<b>the Glutttony facet of the Gift of Hunger</b> <b>already does this</b>), and lodge members with very high Primal Urge can force spirits of hunger to Claim victims (<b>No idea what to do of this</b>)</li> </ol><br /> <br /> <br /> It seems that using the Gift of Hunger, Gift of Essence, Bale Hounds (Hounds of Consumption) <i>Siskur-Dah</i> and PERHAPS Ghost Wolf Devourers you get most of this lodge flavour. But what should be the Aspiration and Ban? What merits should they have? (I think Lodge Lorehouse and Lodge Stronghold are the most apt)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Based on <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1757_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1757\" data-vbnamecard=\"1757\">Acrozatarim</a> post that had<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/798541-alpha-predators-the-strongest-werewolves?p=801351#post801351\"> non-official stats for Lycaon-Ur</a>, this is my take on the leader of the Lodge of the Field using existing rules (Devourers, Gift of Hunger, <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/the-giver-of-gifts-2-werewolf-the-forsaken/\" target=\"_blank\">Gift of Essence</a>)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lycaon-Ur</b><br /> <b>Tribe:</b> Ghost Wolf (Devourer)<br /> <b>Auspice:</b> None<br /> <b>Blood:</b> Alpha<br /> <b>Bone:</b> Guru<br /> <b>Aspirations:</b> Consume human flesh; Achieve spiritual transcendence; Grow the lodge<br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 4, Wits 5, Resolve 6<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 6/7/9/11/6, Dexterity 4/4/5/6/6, Stamina 8/9/10/10/9<br /> <b>Social Attributes: </b>Presence 6, Manipulation 5/4/5/4/4, Composure 2<br /> <b>Mental Skills: </b>Academics 3, Crafts 3, Investigation 4, Medicine 2, Occult 5, Politics 4<br /> <b>Physical Skills: </b>Athletics 4, Brawl (Bite, Claws) 7, Stealth 6, Survival 5, Weaponry 4<br /> <b>Social Skills:</b> Animal Ken 5, Empathy 5, Expression 6, Intimidation (Monstrous) 7, Persuasion 6, Socialize 4, Streetwise 3, Subterfuge 3<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Allies (Lodge of the Field) 5, Dedicated Locus 5, Fetish (Devourer\u2019s Fang) 2, Fortified Form (Gauru, Urshul) 5, Indomitable, Instinctive Defense, Iron Stamina 3, Iron Will, Language (Czech, German, Russian, Silesian, First Tongue; native Polish), Living Weapon (Urshul bite, Urshul claws) 5, Lodge Sorcery 5, Relentless Assault 4, Resources 5, Retainer 4, Safe Place 5, Staff 5, Status (Lodge of the Field) 5, Striking Looks 1, Tactical Shifting 5<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 8<br /> <b>Harmony:</b> 5<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5/6/7/9/4<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 6/6/7/8/8<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 8/8/9/10/10<br /> <b>Armor (Gauru, Urshul):</b> 2/2<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 15/16/19/25/20<br /> <b>Health:</b> 13/15/17/19/13<br /> <b>Primal Urge: </b>10<br /> <b>Renown:</b> Cunning 4, Glory 4, Honor 3, Purity 3, Wisdom 4<br /> <b>Gifts: </b>(Death) Cold Embrace, Barghest, Bone Gnaw; (Dominance) All; (Elementals) Catastrophe, Tongue of Flame; (Essence) All; (Evasion) All; (Hunger) Gluttony, Wolf-Hunger; (Hunting) All; (Insight) Prey on Weakness, Read the World\u2019s Loom, Scent the Unnatural, One Step Ahead; (Stealth) Shadow Pelt, Predator\u2019s Shadow, Running Silent; (Strength) All; (Warding) All; (Weather) Hunt Under Iron Skies; (Change) All; (Pack) Maw of Madness<br /> <b>Rites:</b> Sacred Hunt, Devour, Urfarah\u2019s Bane<br /> <b>Enlightenments:</b> Forge Spawn, Impossible Regeneration, Inviolate Soul, Paragon of Renown (Cunning, Glory), Primal Form, Stainless Harmony<br /> <b>Essence: </b>78/15<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Lycaon-Ur is continually hungry and must spend a point of Essence every day that he goes without consuming human or werewolf flesh.\u200b<br /> <b>Conditions:</b> Addicted (human flesh, werewolf flesh), Cunning, Glorious","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 09-03-2024, 02:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-26T20:21:59-07:00","id":1523195,"title":"","content":"A lodge obsessed with spiritual transcendence and essence gaining seems like they should have lodge sorcery as a merit. Lycan-Ur especially feels like he needs influence: Hunger that Chris gave him. <br /> <br /> If I were to do a post for him I think I would go a different route, he'd be an imposter, probably a balehound or a devourer trying to lead the lodge into corruption.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}